{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"HTTPDestination","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L65"},"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as one request, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends it again until it arrives."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:backoff:clock:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","text":"HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","text":"BatchEncoder"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next batch sent only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once the previous one is delivered or dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The method is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST"},{"type":"text","text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, where a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the batch’s records, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request the transport can never send ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":": a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Retry-After","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the batch, and it isn’t sent again."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A batch the endpoint rejects,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose request can’t be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped: logged at error"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level and reported on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns without logging or reporting it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which drops its oldest batch when full ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":"): offline for long"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enough, the batches dropped there are lost to this run. A store never had them acknowledged,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so it delivers them on the next launch; without a store they are gone."}]},{"code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedBatch/contentType":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"contentType","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"contentType","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedbatch\/contenttype","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The body’s media type, sent as the request’s "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"\"application\/json\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", say."}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"BatchEncoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the body of the request "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransportError/invalidRequest(reason:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransporterror\/invalidrequest(reason:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The transport can never send the request as it is: its URL is malformed or of a scheme the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transport doesn’t support, or the platform refuses it, as App Transport Security refuses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"text":" URL.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"invalidRequest","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"reason","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)","title":"HTTPTransportError